RLS is mandatory.

Enable RLS on every table containing private or business-specific data.

Policies must ensure:

CUSTOMERS:
- Can read public business information.
- Can access only their own anonymous-session queue records.
- Can access only their own order records.
- Cannot access other customers' private information.
- Cannot manipulate queue positions or service statuses.

BUSINESS OWNERS:
- Can access their own business records.
- Can manage authorized business members.
- Can manage their own menu.
- Can manage their own counters.
- Can manage queues belonging to their business.
- Can access orders belonging to their business.
- Cannot access another business owner's private data.

PUBLIC VISITORS:
- Can view permitted public business information.
- Cannot access private customer information.

Do not rely on frontend checks as security.

Create and test RLS policies.

Never expose the Supabase service-role key in frontend code.

Never use VITE_ or other public environment prefixes for service-role credentials.

